<title>SWEDEN: Riksbank signs two new primary dealer agreements.</title>
<headline>Riksbank signs two new primary dealer agreements.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sweden's central bank, the Riksbank, said on Tuesday it had concluded primary dealer agreements with SBC Warburg and Unibank.</p>
<p>The agreement with Unibank in Copenhagen is for the money and bond market, the Riksbank said in a statement.</p>
<p>An agreement with SBC Warburg in Zurich related to the foreign exchange market.</p>
<p>Both agreements come into effect on July 1.</p>
<p>The Riksbank said it now has 10 primary dealers in the foreign exchange market and 11 in the money market.</p>
<p>-- Belinda Goldsmith, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
